epictetus-3.md:1: argue/answered: S9: answered no, which keeps epictetus-3.logic.r1.3, to: Suppose "wherever I go there are the sun, moon, stars, dreams, omens and conversation with gods" is false. Is S9, "But wherever I go, there is the sun, there is the moon, there are the stars, dreams, omens, and the conversation ([Greek: omilia]) with gods.", true then?
epictetus-3.logic.r1: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 2 ways: epictetus-3.logic.r1 has "material_understanding ∧ business_appearances ∧ body_nothing → death_indifferent" and "¬can_eject ∧ same_everywhere → ¬should_fly"; epictetus-3.logic.r1.2 and epictetus-3.logic.r1.3 have "material_understanding ∧ business_appearances → purify_faculty" and "body_nothing → death_indifferent" and "¬can_eject ∧ same_everywhere → ¬should_fly"; they differ when only "you must make your ruling faculty pure, and this mode of life also", "the matter for me to work on is my understanding, as wood is to the carpenter", "the body and its parts are nothing to me", "one should fly (to escape)" and "some man can eject me out of the world" are true, which the first allows
epictetus-3.md:1: argue/readings: the conclusion is read 2 ways: epictetus-3.logic.r1 has "death_indifferent"; epictetus-3.logic.r1.2 and epictetus-3.logic.r1.3 have "purify_faculty"; they differ when only "death, of the whole or of a part, may come when it chooses" is true, which the first allows
epictetus-3.logic.r1: argue/readings: the main conclusion is read at 2 sentences: epictetus-3.logic.r1 puts it at S5, "Let it come when it chooses, either death of the whole or of a part."; epictetus-3.logic.r1.2 and epictetus-3.logic.r1.3 at S1, "In the first place then you must make your ruling faculty pure, and this mode of life also."
epictetus-3.logic.r1: argue/answered: M: answered no, which keeps epictetus-3.logic.r1.2 and epictetus-3.logic.r1.3, to: Is the text's main conclusion S5, "Let it come when it chooses, either death of the whole or of a part.", rather than S1, "In the first place then you must make your ruling faculty pure, and this mode of life also."?
epictetus-3.logic.r1: argue/answers-split: no reading agrees with all 4 answers (epictetus-3.logic.r1 1, epictetus-3.logic.r1.2 1, epictetus-3.logic.r1.3 3 of them): each is right somewhere, and the reading the answers want takes statements from more than one
